+
+The failed assertion shows `3_000_000` base units, i.e. 3 USDT, still held as aUSDT by the vault after accounting says the vault has zero assets and zero shares.
+
+### What I would change
+
+Decide who owns fees and represent that explicitly in accounting. Two reasonable designs:
+
+- If fees belong to a fee recipient, withdraw `grossAssets` from Aave, transfer `netAssets` to the user, and send or account the fee separately.
+- If fees are meant to benefit remaining shareholders, only leave fees in the share pool while `totalShares > 0`; when the last shares are burned, redeem or assign the remaining fee so it cannot become unowned aUSDT.
+
+In either design, add a conservation invariant: when `totalShares == 0`, the vault should not retain aUSDT/USDT unless it is explicitly tracked as protocol fees.
