+### What I would change
+
+Add a custom error and validate both constructor and setter input. I would not use `BPS_DENOMINATOR` itself as the practical max unless a 100% deposit fee is intentionally allowed, because 100% deposits cannot mint shares. A safer bound is an explicit small `MAX_DEPOSIT_FEE_BPS` chosen by governance, with tests for zero, max, max plus one, and constructor validation.
